{"event": "result", "result": {"conversation_id": "e5875ace-a3cd-4aa1-9177-304b20324bf2", "status": "SUCCESS", "response": "I have analyzed the `repo_lock` implementation in `agent_branches/sync_git.py` (since it wasn't in `git_utils.py`) and wrote the findings to the requested JSON file.\n\nHere is a summary of the analysis:\n- **Flock flags:** It correctly uses `fcntl.LOCK_EX | fcntl.LOCK_NB` to attempt a non-blocking exclusive lock.\n- **Backoff polling:** If it fails to acquire the lock (catches `IOError` or `OSError`), it sleeps for 0.05 seconds before retrying.\n- **Timeout & cleanup:** It tracks elapsed time using `time.monotonic()`. If `timeout_sec` (default 10.0s) is exceeded without acquiring the lock, it raises a `SyncGitError`. Finally, it ensures that `fcntl.LOCK_UN` and `os.close(fd)` are safely executed in a `finally` block to prevent resource leaks.\n\nThe report has been saved to:\n[ab-lock-report.json](file:///home/alexey/git/cloudflare-agent-git/.local/scratch/fleet_work/ab-lock-report.json)\n", "duration_seconds": 84.136461164, "num_turns": 1, "usage": {"input_tokens": 76313, "output_tokens": 2424, "thinking_tokens": 1718, "cache_read_tokens": 31347, "total_tokens": 78737}}}
